# This corpus is byte-exact. Its SHA-256 values are the PC-01 acceptance oracle, so any
# end-of-line translation on checkout would corrupt every fixture and every recorded
# digest at once - silently, on the machine that did the checkout and nowhere else.
# Marking the artefacts binary stops Git rewriting a byte and stops it trying to diff one.
#
# It also settles a smaller nuisance: a PDF cross-reference entry is required by the
# format to be exactly twenty bytes ending in a space, so `git diff --check` reports
# "trailing whitespace" on any PDF it mistakes for text. Those spaces are mandated, not
# stray.
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
